{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver never reached the pickup point at all. EV-GPS-00612's driver track reports a minimum distance to the pickup pin of 350.79 m across all 116 fixes, roughly seven times the 50 m arrival radius that POL-NS-02 fixes for a STANDARD zone, and the derived arrival block records qualifying_fix_count 0 with a longest qualifying run of 0 seconds. On POL-NS-02 the driver is not deemed to have arrived, POL-NS-01(b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the cancellation fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and the fee fails on two limbs. Limb (b) requires the gps_trace to place the driver inside the POL-NS-02 geofence at or before the 'arrived' event, and not one fix in EV-GPS-00612 is inside the 50 m radius at any moment of the trip. Limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least 300 seconds for a STANDARD pickup, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and the longest qualifying run is 0 seconds. Where any of limbs (a) to (d) fails the fee is not chargeable, and the amount charged must be refunded rather than left standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived at pickup' marker the driver points to is a false marker under POL-NS-05. At the recorded arrival time of 2026-09-12T08:34:52 the driver's nearest fix was 350.79 m from the pin, past the 300 m threshold, so the marker cannot start the waiting clock. POL-NS-05(ii) then applies with full force: no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, so the fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the trip should be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver in the ruling's referrals list.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300 second STANDARD minimum, so under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present on the road. The accumulator in POL-NS-06(i) cannot rescue the fee here: EV-GPS-00612 shows zero in-geofence intervals to sum (run_count 0, accumulated dwell 0.0 s), and limb (i) in any event requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated. The only advisory, EV-ADVIS-00612-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and I cite it for its absence only: a MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and can never reduce or excuse the shortfall.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-ADVIS-00612-01", "EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.accumulated_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip was not a rider no-show in substance, and POL-NS-01(d) is not made out. The record shows cancelled_by SYSTEM at 08:49:50, not termination by the driver as limb (d) requires. On the substance, EV-TRIP-00612 records a driver-placed in-app call at 08:35:40, answered, running 400 seconds: the driver was in live voice contact with the rider within a minute of his own marker, and his filed statement confirms he told her to rebook because he could not wait. A rider the driver was talking to for six and a half minutes was reachable, so a RIDER_NO_SHOW termination is contradicted by the driver's own conduct on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was at the pin. EV-GPS-00612's rider track places her device between 3.58 m and 13.98 m from the pickup pin across 101 qualifying fixes, mean 8.75 m, comfortably inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius that EV-GPS-00612's own thresholds and POL-NS-04 use for this zone class. The driver's statement that 'the passenger wasn't there' is contradicted by the rider's own telemetry; the party who was not at the pickup point is the driver, 350 m away. I rely on POL-NS-04 only for its presence standard and measurement radius, not for its exoneration route: that route is not available on this record because the chat log is empty and the driver did place an in-app call.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, and even on the most generous reading of the driver's account that he waited near the block, POL-NS-03 gives the same answer: a driver stationary outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius has not arrived at the pickup point, POL-NS-01(b) fails, and the fee is refunded to the rider in full. The pin-ambiguity goodwill limb is not triggered, because EV-TRIP-00612 records registered_pickup_points as 1 and the chat log is empty, so neither sub-location condition in POL-NS-03 can be satisfied on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612", "EV-CHAT-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays only 'where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it'; POL-NS-01 fails on limbs (b) and (c), and POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 both displace the fee. The anti-farming check does not arise, but for completeness driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d is 110, so the rate limb of the POL-NS-07 test could not be met either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-09 escalation is not engaged and the case should be decided, not deferred. Trigger (b) is the only candidate and there is no unresolved contradiction: EV-TRIP-00612's arrival marker is contradicted by EV-GPS-00612, and POL-NS-05 is the clause written to resolve precisely that conflict, so no open question is left for a reviewer. Triggers (c) and (d) read zero: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the POL-NS-07 check does not trip. The deciding artifact EV-GPS-00612 is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 and the bundle carries no policy-level impairment under POL-NS-08, so neither trigger (e) nor the 0.70 confidence floor is reached, and no confidence cap under POL-GEN-02 arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00612", "EV-TRIP-00612", "EV-RPROF-00612", "EV-DPROF-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantum is exact. EV-FARE-00612 charges a single contested line: cancellation_fee 4.00, with base_fare, distance_fare, time_fare, platform_fee, promo_discount, surge and tolls all 0.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The relief sought is therefore SGD 4.00 and nothing further; POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation-fee line only, not any booking or platform fee that would have been charged on a completed trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00612"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.total_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{"claims":[
  {"text":"The rider's quickest route to a refund that carries no driver payment - POL-NS-04 - is closed on this record. Limb (a) requires a chat message from the rider that locates or coordinates; this trip's chat log is empty (message_count 0, first_message_at and last_message_at both null), so no such message exists to rely on. Limb (b) requires that the driver neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds nor placed any in-app voice call before terminating; the trip record shows the driver placed an in-app call at 08:35:40 which was answered and ran 400 seconds. Both limbs fail independently, so the rider cannot be exonerated under this clause and the case must be decided on the ordinary no-show tests.","evidence_ids":["EV-CHAT-00612","EV-TRIP-00612"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-04"],"relies_on":"in_app_calls","asserted_weight":1.0},
  {"text":"The POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not trip on this driver. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the four-or-more limb, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 110 is 0.009, below the 0.08 limb. The check requires both limbs and neither is met, so nothing here supports withholding a driver payment or an abuse finding, and under POL-GEN-01 only those two trailing-window counters may be used for this test - no lifetime counter or rating is substituted for them.","evidence_ids":["EV-DPROF-00612"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-07","POL-GEN-01"],"relies_on":"driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d","asserted_weight":1.0},
  {"text":"On the driver's own telemetry this is not a driver who was somewhere else entirely: all 116 fixes in his trace lie inside POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-location ceiling of the pin, the closest approach being 350.79 m, and the trip record documents a 4.2 minute run to the area (time_to_arrival_min 4.2), a full 15.0 minute hold (wait_time_min 15.0) and an answered in-app call at 08:35:40. The driver was in the pickup vicinity for the entire waiting window; at most this is a wrong-face-of-the-location dispute within the 400 m band, not an abandonment and not a driver who took another job and came back.","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00612","EV-TRIP-00612"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.driver_track.min_distance_m","asserted_weight":1.0},
  {"text":"If the judge cannot reconcile the trip record - which asserts an arrival event at 08:34:52, a RIDER_NO_SHOW termination and a 15.0 minute wait - with a trace that never comes closer than 350.79 m to the pin and yields zero qualifying in-geofence fixes and zero measured dwell, then two admissible artifacts stand in direct contradiction on arrival, which is the situation POL-NS-09(b) describes. On that footing the disputed SGD 4.00 should be held for human review rather than released by the automated pipeline.","evidence_ids":["EV-TRIP-00612","EV-GPS-00612"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-09"],"relies_on":"derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count","asserted_weight":1.0}
]}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record TRP-00612 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-31205 — the 'arrived at pickup' marker timestamped 2026-09-12T08:34:52 was set while the driver's nearest GPS fix (EV-GPS-00612) was 350.79 m from the pickup pin, beyond the 300 m threshold, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on TRP-00612 is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-00612) charges one line — cancellation_fee SGD 4.00 — on a STANDARD pickup (Blk 27 Kallang Bahru) in a RYDE_X vehicle. The charge needs POL-NS-01 to hold in full, and on the driver's own telemetry (EV-GPS-00612, COMPLETE, weight 1.0, 116 fixes at 10 s cadence, no gaps) it fails two limbs. Limb (b): the trace never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at any point — the closest of all 116 fixes is 350.79 m from the pin (mean 377.20 m). Limb (c): in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum (qualifying_fix_count 0; longest qualifying run 0 s). Limb (d) is also doubtful: the record shows cancelled_by SYSTEM rather than termination by the driver, though the reason code reads RIDER_NO_SHOW. On POL-NS-02, the absence of any qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation means the driver is not deemed to have arrived. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result independently: 0 s of effective dwell against a 300 s minimum. And the driver's 'arrived at pickup' marker at 08:34:52 is a FALSE marker under POL-NS-05 — at that moment his nearest fix was 350.79 m from the pin, past the 300 m threshold (clock skew is 2 s, well inside POL-NS-08(a)) — and POL-NS-05(ii) applies because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip.\n\nThe rider's position. The rider's own device (rider track in EV-GPS-00612) is placed 3.58 m to 13.98 m from the pin across 101 fixes, mean 8.75 m, inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. She was at the pickup; the driver's statement that 'the passenger wasn't there' is not supported by the telemetry, and his own filed statement concedes he told her to rebook and could not wait.\n\nThe driver's arguments, answered. (1) POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider — the chat log (EV-CHAT-00612) is empty and the driver placed an answered 400-second in-app call at 08:35:40 — but that clause is not the route to this refund; the refund follows from POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06. (2) A wrong-entrance reading under POL-NS-03 would not help either: POL-NS-03 also refunds the rider in full, and its pin-ambiguity goodwill cannot arise because registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more, so no driver payment flows from it — and in any event the driver was not held within the 400 m band (fixes range 350.79–567.28 m). (3) No driver compensation is payable under POL-NS-07, which pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; it is not. The anti-farming check is correctly not tripped (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1/110 = 0.009, below 0.08), but that is immaterial because the payout precondition already fails. (4) Escalation under POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged: the trip record's arrival marker and the GPS trace do pull against each other on arrival, but POL-NS-05 is precisely the clause written to resolve that conflict, so no open question is left for a reviewer. No other trigger fires — confidence is above the 0.70 floor, disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and 0, no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the deciding artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no POL-NS-08 impairment; the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee equals the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (SGD 4.00), so limb (d) is clean.\n\nReferral. Under POL-NS-05(ii) the trip is referred for recording as a false-arrival event against the driver. The disputed SGD 4.00 is refunded, not held, and the rider's charge is discharged in full."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-31205 on trip TRP-00612 in the platform's false-arrival register, the 'arrived' marker at 2026-09-12T08:34:52 having been entered at a point more than 300 m from the pickup pin with no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe waiting period the fee pays for never happened. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00612) says the driver marked 'arrived' at 08:34:52 and that the platform recorded a 15.0 minute wait, but the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00612 — 116 fixes at 10-second cadence, complete, no sampling gap) never places the driver closer than 350.79 m to the pickup pin, and much of the window sits further out. The pickup zone class is STANDARD, so the arrival radius is 50 m. Across the whole trace there are zero qualifying in-geofence fixes (qualifying_fix_count 0) and the longest continuous in-geofence run is 0 seconds against the 300-second minimum dwell. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive, and limbs (b) and (c) both fail: the driver was not inside the geofence at or before the 'arrived' event, and he never held position there for 300 seconds. Limb (d) is not made out either — the termination is recorded as cancelled_by SYSTEM, and it cannot be 'at or after the required dwell' when no in-geofence dwell ever elapsed.\n\nBecause the 'arrived' marker falls at a moment when the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin, POL-NS-05 makes that marker FALSE. There is no clock-skew problem (the nearest fix is 2 seconds from the marker, far inside the 90-second threshold) and speed is not the trigger here (maximum 5.0 km/h); the distance limb is. Recomputing the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, there is no such fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: refund in full, no compensation, and a false-arrival referral against the driver. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result on its own — effective dwell 0 s against the 300-second STANDARD minimum — and limb (i) cannot rescue the fee: there are no in-geofence intervals to sum, and the only advisory, EV-ADVIS-00612-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0 and is cited for its absence only, carrying no fact (POL-GEN-02 narration therefore does not bite on it). POL-NS-02 gives the same answer directly: no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation.\n\nThe driver's escalation argument under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected. The trip record and the trace do collide on arrival, but a clause resolves that very collision: POL-NS-05 is written for a marker the trace contradicts. No other trigger fires — the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1/110 = 0.009, below 0.08, and per POL-GEN-01 only those two counters were used, not rating or any lifetime counter — the referee's flag on the word 'rating' is context-only and no context-only field was used as a ground); both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d): no gap over 120 s, 116 fixes, the rider track is present, the chat log is consistent with chat_message_count 0, and the 4.00 fee equals the greater of the 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the 4.00 RYDE_X tier fee.\n\nThe rider is right that the driver's own phone call shows she was reachable — a 400-second answered in-app call at 08:35:40 — but POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her by that route: limb (a) fails because the chat log is empty (0 messages), and limb (b) fails because the driver did place that call. That makes no difference, because the outcome rests on the driver's own telemetry. Her presence is nonetheless established independently: her track sits 3.58–13.98 m from the pin (mean 8.75 m) across 101 fixes, well inside the 100 m STANDARD radius, so the driver's statement that 'the passenger wasn't there' is not borne out. POL-NS-03, if reached, gives the same full refund and triggers no goodwill payment, because registered_pickup_points is 1 and the chat is empty. POL-NS-07 pays nothing: it requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which it is not.\n\nAmount: SGD 4.00, read from EV-FARE-00612 (cancellation_fee 4.00; total_charged 4.00; base, distance, time, platform, surge and toll lines all 0.00; payment_status CHARGED; refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Only the cancellation-fee line is refunded. Confidence is 0.95: every artifact carrying the deciding facts (EV-GPS-00612, EV-TRIP-00612) is at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-00612 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-31205 - the 08:34:52 'arrived' marker was set while the driver's own trace placed him 350.79 m from the pickup pin, and the trip contains zero qualifying in-geofence fixes."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged on EV-FARE-00612 (cancellation_fee 4.00; payment_status CHARGED; refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded in full to the rider. The contested amount is the cancellation-fee line only; no booking or platform fee was charged on this trip.\n\nThe fee cannot stand under POL-NS-01, which is conjunctive. The driver's own trace EV-GPS-00612 never brings him within the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius fixed by POL-NS-02: across 116 fixes his closest approach to the pin is 350.79 m (mean 377.20 m, maximum 567.28 m), and the derived arrival block records qualifying_fix_count 0 and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0 seconds. Limb (b) fails (no in-geofence fix at or before the 08:34:52 'arrived' event) and limb (c) fails (no continuous 300-second dwell for a STANDARD zone). POL-NS-01's own text says the fee is then not chargeable and the refund is decided under POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 or POL-NS-06.\n\nAll three give the same answer. POL-NS-02: there is no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes preceding the 08:49:50 cancellation, so the driver never arrived and the rider is entitled to a full refund. POL-NS-05: at the 08:34:52 'arrived' timestamp the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, so the marker is FALSE; and because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full, pays no compensation, and records a false-arrival event against the driver - that referral is carried below. POL-NS-06: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so the fee is not chargeable. The POL-NS-06(i) accumulator cannot rescue it: there are zero in-geofence intervals to sum, and the only advisory, EV-ADVIS-00612-01, is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), which makes limb (i) unavailable rather than excusing the shortfall.\n\nDriver's points. (1) He says he arrived and waited; his 'arrived' entry is a status only (POL-NS-05), and trip_record.wait_time_min of 15.0 cannot create an arrival his own telemetry shows never happened. (2) He argues POL-NS-03 keeps this inside the 400 m wrong-location band, so at most a wrong-face dispute. Two answers: his assertion that all 116 fixes lie within 400 m is contradicted by his own trace (maximum distance 567.28 m), and in any event POL-NS-03 also refunds the rider in full - it bears only on driver compensation, and its pin-ambiguity limb (ii) cannot supply any because trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more, while the empty chat log EV-CHAT-00612 leaves limb (i) unreachable. (3) He argues POL-NS-09(b) escalation because the trip record and the trace conflict on arrival. That is precisely the conflict POL-NS-05 is written to resolve, so no open question is left for a reviewer. Triggers (c), (d) and (e) also do not fire: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0; no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 110, well under both anti-farming limbs; and no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d) - the trace has 116 fixes, zero gaps and no clock skew against the arrival or termination timestamps, the chat log is consistent with chat_message_count 0, and the fare reconciles under the resolution rule (greater of the STANDARD zone fee 4.00 and the RYDE_X tier fee 4.00 = 4.00).\n\nRider's points. Her POL-NS-04 exoneration route is indeed closed on this record - the chat log is empty, so limb (a) has no locating or coordinating message, and the driver's answered 400-second in-app call at 08:35:40 defeats limb (b) - but it is not needed, because the refund follows independently from POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06. Her rider-track (101 fixes, 3.58 to 13.98 m from the pin, mean 8.75 m) confirms she was at the pickup point, and the driver's statement that she was not there is outweighed by it. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-01 is not satisfied, and POL-NS-05(ii), POL-NS-06 and POL-NS-03 each withhold it.\n\nConfidence rests on EV-GPS-00612 and EV-TRIP-00612, both at weight_multiplier 1.0; the only sub-1.0 artifact, EV-ADVIS-00612-01 at 0.0, is cited for its absence alone and carries no deciding fact. The confidence floor of 0.70 is comfortably cleared, so no escalation arises."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
